  "id": "Compound::DB00294 - Gene::2099",
  "verbalization": "Etonogestrel is linked to Esr1 through a shared pathway involving progesterone congeners, with Etonogestrel and Norgestimate both classified under Progesterone Congeners. This class of compounds binds to Esr1, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving estrogen receptor activation. The evidence is further supported by the inclusion of Etonogestrel in Progesterone Congeners and its binding to Esr1, with the lowest common ancestor of these entities being Progestin. The relationship between Etonogestrel and Esr1 is thus mediated through the progesterone congener pathway, where the compound's structural similarity to progesterone allows it to interact with the estrogen receptor. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Etonogestrel in modulating estrogen receptor signaling, though the exact mechanism of binding and its clinical implications remain to be fully elucidated.",
